\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.1}{\ignorespaces Observational constraints and ESA Euclid forecast. (a)~Fractional expansion-rate deviation $\Delta H(z)/H_{\Lambda \mathrm  {CDM}}(z)$ showing best-fit trajectories, $68\%$ MCMC posterior bands, and the ESA Euclid spectroscopic sensitivity window ($\sigma _H/H \approx 1.3\%$ per bin across $0.9 \le z \le 1.8$~\cite  {blanchard2020}). (b)~Reconstructed dark energy equation of state $w(z)$. While CPL plunges monotonically into phantom values ($w(3) = -1.277$), the Log-Oscillatory model exhibits a turnaround ($w(3) = -1.172$, $\Delta w = +0.104$). (c)~Progressive model-selection criteria ($\Delta \chi ^2$, $\Delta \mathrm  {AIC}$, $\Delta \mathrm  {BIC}$) across dataset combinations.}}{13}{figure.3.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:forecast}{{3.1}{13}{Observational constraints and ESA Euclid forecast. (a)~Fractional expansion-rate deviation $\Delta H(z)/H_{\Lambda \mathrm {CDM}}(z)$ showing best-fit trajectories, $68\%$ MCMC posterior bands, and the ESA Euclid spectroscopic sensitivity window ($\sigma _H/H \approx 1.3\%$ per bin across $0.9 \le z \le 1.8$~\cite {blanchard2020}). (b)~Reconstructed dark energy equation of state $w(z)$. While CPL plunges monotonically into phantom values ($w(3) = -1.277$), the Log-Oscillatory model exhibits a turnaround ($w(3) = -1.172$, $\Delta w = +0.104$). (c)~Progressive model-selection criteria ($\Delta \chi ^2$, $\Delta \mathrm {AIC}$, $\Delta \mathrm {BIC}$) across dataset combinations}{figure.3.1}{}}
